FINAL ANSWER:
Ask **hakanensari**, **Gonzalo Rodriguez** and **Divya Rao**. I ranked them by surviving lines in `lib/rack/attack/store_proxy` (7 files, 332 of 346 lines attributed, using `git blame -w -M -C` as of 2026-04-14).

| Person | Lines | Share | Commits | Last commit | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| hakanensari | 74 | 22.3% | 1 | 2014-04-15 | inactive |
| Gonzalo Rodriguez | 59 | 17.8% | 24 | 2026-03-09 | active |
| Divya Rao | 53 | 16.0% | 1 | 2026-01-28 | active |
| Hye-jin Park | 31 | 9.3% | 2 | 2026-02-20 | active |
| Brad Lindsay | 25 | 7.5% | 1 | 2018-02-06 | inactive |

The remaining 18 authors hold the other lines. The `active` marker means a commit in the year before 2026-04-14. It does not change the order.

**Who to ask and who to put on the PR**
- **Gonzalo Rodriguez** is the practical first contact. They hold the second-most lines, made 24 commits, and committed most recently. Gonzalo also appears as "Gonzalo" under the same address, and that name is already counted in the 59 lines.
- **Divya Rao** is the second active owner, with 53 lines from a single commit in January 2026.
- **hakanensari** wrote the original code, with 74 lines, and made the first commit on 2014-04-15. They haven't committed in over a year, so they are unlikely to review. Hye-jin Park (31 lines, active) is the next active person if you want a third reviewer.

**Caveats**
- **Bus factor:** it is 3, meaning 3 authors hold 56.0% of the surviving lines. Reaching 80% takes 7 authors. Both figures cover only `lib/rack/attack/store_proxy`, and they measure how concentrated the remaining code is, not who understands it.
- **Excluded:** one bot identity (14 lines, 1 commit) is left out. No reformat commits were set aside.
- **Mechanical rewrites:** I checked for them and set aside 0. One commit looks mechanical and I kept it: `20d6682` "style: fix Lint/HandleExceptions rubocop" by Gonzalo Rodriguez, 2 surviving lines.
- **Copy detection:** the figures use `-C` copy detection. It credits lines moved between files to the original authors. 37 of 346 lines (10.7%) were moved or copied into this directory from other paths. Without copy detection, hakanensari has 55 lines (16.6%) and Gonzalo has 52 (15.7%), so both stay in the top three. Mei Tanaka goes from 11 lines (3.3%) with it to 42 (12.7%) without, so they hold more than the table suggests. Mei Tanaka may be worth a look as well, because the table credits them with only 11 lines.
- **Possible duplicate identity:** Jonathan del Strother appears under two addresses (<email redacted> and <email redacted>). The tool rates this strong, so I'd count them as one person, with 19 lines (5.7%) combined. That is a guess from names and addresses until you confirm it. It doesn't change the top three, and I haven't written anything to `.mailmap`.

Line counts show whose code is still here. They don't capture design input or review work, and code that was deleted counts for nobody.
